\begin{align*}
8x + 2a &= 7x + 2b\\
x &= 2b - 2a.
\end{align*}
The area of the first triangle is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 8x \cdot \sqrt{a^2 - (4x)^2}$, and the area of the second triangle is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 7x \cdot \sqrt{b^2 - (3.5x)^2}$. Since the areas are equal, we have
\begin{align*}
